  "notes": "Catalog document covering many part numbers and form factors; optical parameters vary per row. Temperature options stated as commercial (0°C to 70°C), extended (-10°C to 85°C), or industrial (-40°C to 85°C) without per-SKU assignment. Data rates include OC-n (155, 622 Mb/s), 1.25 G, 2.5 G, ~10 G (9.9-11.3, 10.3125, 10.313), 40 G (39.8-44.8, 41.25), 100 G (103.1-111.8). Wavelength columns include single nm, BIDI pairs (e.g. 1310/1490), and ranges (1270-1610, 1470-1610, 1295-1310, 1270-1330). Distances include m and km (100 m, 220/500 m, 220 m, 300 m, 2 km, etc.). Copper SFP-T models use Cat 5 with no TX/RX dBm values. GPON models list asymmetric rates 1.25/2.5 and 2.5/1.25. CXP-SR10 lists rate 12.7-126 (as printed). Link Budget column values not mapped to schema fields. Return rate 0.010% and failure rate 0.0029% are quality metrics, not transceiver specs.",
